comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-11T06:19:11.614Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete live all-status PM inventory has 2732 items with complete source receipts and no omissions; keyword searches for issue numbers and policy authoring/completeness/ownership concepts found no dedicated issue. Existing delivered feature and recovery lineage retained. GitHub has no open PRs or Dependabot/code-scanning alerts; three open reports already have canonical PM link comments."
  "2026-09-11T06:25:49.176Z","harness:codex","TDD and integration evidence: the initial new completeness and policy-id regressions both failed before implementation. All 53 focused tests now pass, including real CLI and MCP policy-id normalization, an assurance floor that fails with no policy, passes with an applicable policy and fails after deletion, and installed governance-audit append flags preserving assignment while edits/deletes refuse. Complete-population duplicate check and the delivered historical foundations are recorded. Full repository coverage, static gates, temporary manual acceptance and hosted review remain required."
  "2026-09-11T06:30:53.449Z","harness:codex","Verified package implementation: governance-audit already registers --allow-audit-comment for notes/comments/learnings and maps it to the narrow SDK append bypass. The refusal now names both installation and retry flag. Strict defaults and assignment remain unchanged; real installed-package tests reject edit/delete with the append flag. Independent temporary compiled-CLI acceptance passed."
  "2026-09-11T06:39:32.418Z","harness:codex","Recovery acceptance correction: claim is atomic test-and-set, not an implicit takeover. The strict-ownership integration negative control proved that a reader claim fails while writer owns the item. Guidance now requires current-owner release followed by new-owner claim. Package installation plus command help discovers the optional append bypass without leaking package-owned flags into bare-core contracts; edits/deletes remain protected. The package-boundary gate remains unchanged."
  "2026-09-11T06:58:22.791Z","harness:codex","Final manual acceptance in an independent disposable project passed: strict cross-owner annotation refused; held-item claim refused; current-owner release followed by new-owner claim succeeded; append succeeded after handoff; operand-only policy detected missing body, then validation passed after body restoration; history verification passed. Full static quality passed, final ownership ESLint and package-boundary checks passed, and structural docstrings remain exactly 100 percent for source/exported/member contracts. Coverage is being rerun without concurrent builds after an overlapping-build fixture copy race."
  "2026-09-11T06:58:59.751Z","harness:codex","Local implementation verification complete: 8706 tests across 667 files passed; exact coverage 64172/64172 statements, 48869/48869 branches, 13337/13337 functions and 61480/61480 lines. Static quality, typecheck, generated contracts, SDK snapshot, package boundary, docs and exact 100 percent source/export/member docstrings passed. Manual temporary acceptance and linked tests passed. Hosted PR review, analyzer checks and merge remain delivery gates; this closure records implemented behavior, not publication."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-11T06:45:36.501Z","harness:codex","Merge-safe annotations and ownership are independent guarantees: concurrent appends can use the installed governance-audit package without ownership transfer; a real handoff requires current-owner release before atomic claim. Execute every advertised recovery path as an integration test."
